From d68db2b5286f525081c2a54a0cc6631750879c94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:58:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] evidence: ship the receipts the published documents actually
 cite, with a manifest

60 files: 12 named receipts plus the 47 R73 gate cells and the S-X8 provenance record. The citation list is EXTRACTED from README.md and the two release documents rather than hand-written, so the manifest cannot drift from what the release claims. MISSING: none - every cited receipt was located.

MANIFEST.md maps each file to the claim it supports, its original lane path, and the sha256 of the ORIGINAL. Where the path scrub changed a file it says so and carries the shipped copy's own sha256 too, because a verifier hashing the shipped file must not be able to mistake a scrub for tampering. Scrub: user-home paths, studio paths and e-mail addresses only; nothing measured was altered.

This closes the gap the phase-1 branch disclosed: the story's headline receipts were not tracked at any revision, so the curated folder held a single file.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - evidence files and an index; no code path is touched.
