+R58 lane-244 - ENUMERATION RECEIPT: Vulkan memory heaps, memory types, and the memory type every
+buffer class of the 27B S-X8 load actually lands in on the Beelink SER7 Pro (Radeon 780M).
+
+SOURCES (no new box time was spent; both are pre-existing CHECKED receipts):
+  A. `vulkaninfo` VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties, read 2026-09-15 (instance/device creation only,
+     no allocation, no GPU work). Raw: r58-evidence/vulkaninfo-memprops-raw.txt
+  B. R51 lane-240 GGML_VK_ALLOC_TRACE=1 load of the 27B S-X8,
+     <repo>/cache/r51-spill-wt/r51-evidence/30-planorder.txt (99034 lines), which carries both
+     the engine's own memtype enumeration and, per buffer, `state=planned type=T heap=H`.
+  The two agree line for line, so this receipt needed no load cell of its own.
+
+DEVICE: Vulkan0, uma=1, prefer_host=0, max_buffer_size=2147483648 (2 GiB)   [source B, preamble]
+
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+1. HEAPS
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+  heap 0   22,623,813,632 B (21.07 GiB)  DEVICE_LOCAL | MULTI_INSTANCE     budget 21,492,623,360 B
+  heap 1   11,311,906,816 B (10.54 GiB)  (no flags)                        budget 10,746,311,680 B
+  heap 2      268,435,456 B (256.0 MiB)  DEVICE_LOCAL | MULTI_INSTANCE     budget    255,013,680 B
+
+  REFUTATION of the brief/register framing: heap 0 is 21.07 GiB, NOT the 16 GiB BIOS reservation -
+  the driver already exposes ~5 GiB more DEVICE_LOCAL than the carve. Heap 1 is 10.54 GiB, not the
+  ~15.86 GiB "dynamic shared ceiling" the equipment register implies. Total 31.6 GiB. Stated as an
+  observation only; UMA/BIOS changes are the President's alone and none is proposed here.
+
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+2. MEMORY TYPES, AND WHICH ARE ELIGIBLE AT ALL
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+  16 types are enumerated (0-7 mirrored as 8-15). But EVERY storage buffer this engine creates
+  reports VkMemoryRequirements::memoryTypeBits = 0xf (source B, every `state=attempt` line, 46 of
+  46). Only memory types 0,1,2,3 can therefore ever hold our weights. Types 4-15 - including every
+  AMD DEVICE_COHERENT / DEVICE_UNCACHED variant - are enumeration noise for this workload.
+
+  idx  heap  flags                                                        eligible (typeBits 0xf)
+  ---  ----  -----------------------------------------------------------  -----------------------
+    0     0  DEVICE_LOCAL                                                 YES
+    1     1  HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT                                 YES
+    2     2  DEVICE_LOCAL | HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT                  YES
+    3     1  HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT | HOST_CACHED                   YES
+    4     0  DEVICE_LOCAL | DEVICE_COHERENT_AMD | DEVICE_UNCACHED_AMD     no
+    5     1  HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT | DEVICE_COHERENT_AMD | DEVICE_UNCACHED_AMD    no
+    6     2  DEVICE_LOCAL | HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT | DEVICE_COHERENT_AMD | ...     no
+    7     1  HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT | HOST_CACHED | DEVICE_COHERENT_AMD | ...      no
+   8-15     exact mirrors of types 0-7                                    no
+
+  VERDICT: BEYOND THE RESERVATION THERE ARE EXACTLY TWO USABLE MEMORY TYPES.
+    type 1 - HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT                (uncached / write-combined)
+    type 3 - HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT | HOST_CACHED  (snooped, CPU-cached)
+  Both sit on heap 1. That is the whole lever this lane has, and it is a real one: type 3 is
+  already in production use on this box for the transfer/staging buffers (7 allocations,
+  27,695,584 B, source B), so the driver demonstrably serves it - it has simply never carried
+  weights.
+
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+3. WHICH TYPE EACH BUFFER CLASS GETS TODAY - and WHY
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+  Aggregate over the whole S-X8 load (source B, 46 successful allocations):
+
+  class                              allocs           bytes   memtype  heap  flags
+  ---------------------------------  ------  --------------   -------  ----  --------------------------
+  weights, device-local                  23  23,223,063,296         0     0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+  weights, HOST SPLIT                     5   3,281,736,960         1     1  HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+  KV / small tensors                     11     196,109,596         2     2  DL|HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+  staging / transfer                      7      27,695,584         3     1  HV|HC|HOST_CACHED
+
+  WHY the host split lands in type 1 - it is ENUMERATION ORDER, never a measurement:
+  ggml_vk_placement_attempts() (ggml-vulkan.cpp, UMA branch) offers the required-flag passes
+  { DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT }, { DEVICE_LOCAL }, { HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT }.
+    pass 1 (DL|HV|HC) matches only types 2/6/10/14, all on the 256 MiB heap 2 -> structurally dead
+           for GiB-sized weight blocks. (It is alive for the small KV tensors, which is exactly why
+           those land in type 2.)
+    pass 2 (DL) matches types 0/4/8/12 on heap 0 -> takes every block until heap 0 is full.
+    pass 3 (HV|HC) matches types 1 and 3 on heap 1. ggml_vk_find_memory_properties() walks memory
+           types in ASCENDING INDEX, and the planner deduplicates keeping the FIRST position, so
+           type 1 beats type 3 purely because 1 < 3. Nothing measured it.
+
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+4. PER-BUFFER RECEIPT of the S-X8 load (the table HQ asked for)
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+  Join of source B's `plan order i/N: <name> <bytes> B` lines (R51's named-plan receipt, lane-240
+  commit 251b7e3f7) to the `state=planned type=T heap=H` line of the same plan entry.
+  NOTE on names: one plan entry is one ~1 GB SUBALLOCATION BLOCK, and the name printed is the
+  FIRST tensor in that block - not the only tensor in it.
+
+  batch entry  name                                 bytes  memtype heap  flags
+  ----- -----  ---------------------------- -------------  ------- ----  --------------------------
+      0     0  cache_r_l0                       627572736        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     0  output_norm.weight                   20480        2    2  DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+      1     1  output.weight                   1191936000        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     2  blk.0.attn_norm.weight          1038307968        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     3  blk.2.ffn_up.weight             1026481920        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     4  blk.5.ffn_down.weight           1026481920        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     5  blk.8.ffn_gate.weight           1071044352        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     6  blk.11.attn_v.weight            1037623040        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     7  blk.14.attn_qkv.weight          1026440960        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     8  blk.16.ffn_up.weight            1026481920        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1     9  blk.19.ffn_down.weight          1038307968        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    10  blk.22.ffn_gate.weight          1042506624        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    11  blk.25.attn_gate.weight         1054334720        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    12  blk.28.attn_qkv.weight          1038267008        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    13  blk.30.ffn_up.weight            1026481920        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    14  blk.33.ffn_down.weight          1026481920        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    15  blk.36.ffn_gate.weight          1071044352        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    16  blk.39.attn_v.weight            1037623040        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    17  blk.42.attn_qkv.weight          1026440960        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    18  blk.44.ffn_up.weight            1026481920        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    19  blk.47.ffn_down.weight          1038307968        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    20  blk.50.ffn_gate.weight          1042506624        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    21  blk.53.attn_gate.weight         1054334720        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      1    22  blk.56.attn_qkv.weight          1038267008        1    1  HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+      1    23  blk.58.ffn_up.weight            1026481920        1    1  HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+      1    24  blk.61.ffn_down.weight           903201664        1    1  HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+      2     0  cache_k_l3                        33554432        2    2  DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+      3     0  cache_r_l0                       627572736        0    0  DEVICE_LOCAL
+      4     0  (unnamed)                        156893184        1    1  HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+      5     0  (unnamed)                        156893184        1    1  HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT
+
+  READING IT:
+  * HOST SPLIT = the three rows at memtype 1 / heap 1 in batch 1 (blk.56.attn_qkv.weight,
+    blk.58.ffn_up.weight, blk.61.ffn_down.weight) = 2,967,950,592 B, plus the two 156,893,184 B
+    single-buffer batches 4 and 5 = 313,786,368 B. Total on the host path 3,281,736,960 B - which
+    matches the independent aggregate in section 3 exactly.
+  * output.weight (1,191,936,000 B) is DEVICE-LOCAL (batch 1 entry 1, memtype 0 heap 0).
+  * cache_r_l0, the DFlash2 recurrent state (627,572,736 B), is DEVICE-LOCAL (batches 0 and 3,
+    memtype 0 heap 0).
+    -> Both CORRECT the brief's "THE GAP" paragraph, which claimed output.weight and the recurrent
+       cache land on the host-visible path. They do not. HQ's correction is confirmed byte-for-byte
+       by this join.
+  * The two `(unnamed)` 156,893,184 B buffers (batches 4 and 5): owner INFERRED, stated as such.
+    They are single-buffer plan batches appearing only after ~24,550 compute submissions (source B
+    lines 98196 and 98609), long past model load, and they carry no tensor name because a
+    ggml-alloc compute-graph buffer is a raw backend buffer, not a named ctx tensor. That makes
+    them the Vulkan0 COMPUTE-GRAPH buffer being reserved and re-reserved mid-run. The receipt does
+    not name them and this lane spent no box time to prove it: treat the owner as UNRECEIPTED.
+    They matter because they are touched every token and they are on the host path.
+
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+5. CORRECTNESS NOTE
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+  Every eligible heap-1 type (1 and 3) carries HOST_COHERENT. Moving the host split from type 1 to
